# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sign-in configuration — copy to .env.local (local) or set in the build
# pipeline (hosted). Vite bakes these in at BUILD time; changing them needs a
# rebuild. Nothing here is secret — the Entra client secret lives only in the
# hosting platform's app settings, never in this repo or the app bundle.
# Full setup: docs/sso-setup.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# none  — no sign-in; the app opens as before (default)
# swa   — Azure Static Web Apps / App Service built-in Entra auth
# mock  — DEVELOPMENT ONLY: simulate the platform to test the sign-in screens
VITE_AUTH_PROVIDER=none

# Optional: an Entra app role the user must hold (e.g. taxonomy.user).
# Leave empty to admit any user the platform signs in — Entra's
# "Assignment required" on the enterprise app already limits who that is.
VITE_AUTH_REQUIRED_ROLE=

# mock only — which situation to simulate:
#   signed-in | signed-out | no-role | error
VITE_AUTH_MOCK_STATE=signed-in
